-- title:
--   Integral cusp form with Eisenstein Hecke eigenvalues modulo m
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $m$ a natural number with $2 \le m$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid p$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid p$, and let $\pi =$ `heckeProj p` be the ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{T}^{\mathrm{abs}} = \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ to $\mathbb{T}$ sending $X_\ell$ to $U_\ell$ if $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise; the Eisenstein ideal is the kernel of the evaluation $\mathbb{T}^{\mathrm{abs}} \to \mathbb{Z}$ with $X_\ell \mapsto 1$ for $\ell \mid p$ and $X_\ell \mapsto 1 + \ell$ otherwise. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralBasis p`](def/CuspForm_IntegralLattice.html#L17), i.e. the forms in $S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients lie in the image of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ span $S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$ over $\mathbb{C}$; and assume that an integer $c$ is divisible by $m$ whenever its image in $\mathbb{T}$ lies in the ideal generated by $\pi$ of the Eisenstein ideal together with $m$. Then there exist such an integrally $q$-expanded form $f$ and integers $a_n$ with $a_n$ equal, in $\mathbb{C}$, to the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $f$ for every $n$, such that $a_1$ is coprime to $m$ in $\mathbb{Z}$, such that $a_{n\ell} + [\ell \mid n]\,\ell\,a_{n/\ell} \equiv (1+\ell)a_n \pmod m$ for every prime $\ell \ne p$ and every $n \ne 0$, and such that $a_{np} \equiv a_n \pmod m$ for every $n \ne 0$.
--
--   This is the duality step in Mazur's computation of the index of the Eisenstein ideal: the $a_1$-pairing between the weight-two Hecke algebra of $\Gamma_0(p)$ and the lattice of integrally $q$-expanded cusp forms converts a character of $\mathbb{T}$ killing the Eisenstein ideal into an integral cusp form whose Hecke eigenvalues are the Eisenstein ones modulo $m$ and whose first coefficient is a unit modulo $m$. It feeds the congruence between these coefficients and sums of divisors prime to $p$, and thence the determination of elements of the Eisenstein ideal with prescribed image under the projection.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_qIntegral_eisenstein_eigen_mod_of_injective.lean

